.TH SDL_HINT_MAC_OPTION_AS_ALT 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_MAC_OPTION_AS_ALT \- A variable controlling whether the Option key on macOS should be remapped to act as the Alt key.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_MAC_OPTION_AS_ALT \(dqSDL_MAC_OPTION_AS_ALT\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dqnone\(dq: The Option key is not remapped to Alt\[char46] (default)
.PP
\(bu \(dqonly_left\(dq: Only the left Option key is remapped to Alt\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dqonly_right\(dq: Only the right Option key is remapped to Alt\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dqboth\(dq: Both Option keys are remapped to Alt\[char46]
.PP
This will prevent the triggering of key compositions that rely on the Option key, but will still send the Alt modifier for keyboard events\[char46] In the case that both Alt and Option are pressed, the Option key will be ignored\[char46] This is particularly useful for applications like terminal emulators and graphical user interfaces (GUIs) that rely on Alt key functionality for shortcuts or navigation\[char46] This does not apply to
.BR SDL_GetKeyFromScancode
and only has an effect if IME is enabled\[char46]
.PP
This hint can be set anytime\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

